    "factsheet": [
        {
            "heading": "Tour scope",
            "paragraphs": [
                "Step inside Tipping Point East, a circular construction and skills hub in Silvertown, and see the work of the docks' next chapter in action. This free tour gives you direct access to a live site: material storage and processing, workshops, training spaces and demonstrator projects, all part of an ongoing experiment in building differently.",
                "You'll be guided through:",
                "An introduction to Tipping Point East, how it came about and what it's working towards\nThe work of our three founding organisations: RESOLVE Collective, Yes Make and Material Cultures\nA walk around the site's three work areas: the Material Store, Material Yard and Material Library\nTime for questions",
                "Along the way you'll get a feel for:",
                "How the site is governed, funded and run in partnership\nHow materials move through the site, from reclamation to reuse\nHow reuse and bio-based materials shape design decisions\nWhat material justice means in practice",
                "Tours run for up to 90 minutes and are free to attend as part of Open House 2026.",
                "A few things to know before you visit:",
                "We're a working site, so please wear closed-toe shoes and clothing suited to being outdoors\nBring a water bottle"
            ]
        }
    ],
